   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Resultado de hoy",
    "@en": "Today's outcome"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Con **have** + participio, hablas de algo pasado que **sigue afectando hoy**: **I've lost my keys** = he perdido mis llaves (no las encuentro ahora).",
     "@en": "With **have** + participle, you talk about something past that **sigue afectando hoy**: **I've lost my keys** = I have lost my keys (I can't find them now)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Compara: **I lost my keys yesterday** = perdí mis llaves ayer (pasado simple, con cuándo).",
     "@en": "Compare: **I lost my keys yesterday** = I lost my keys yesterday (simple past with when)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Negativa y preguntas",
    "@en": "Negative and Questions"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Negativa: **haven't** / **hasn't** + participio: **She hasn't called** (no ha llamado). Pregunta: **Has he finished?** / **Have they arrived?**",
     "@en": "Negative: **haven't** / **hasn't** + partition: **She hasn't called** (not called). Question: **Has he finished?** / **Have they arrived?**"
    },
    {
     "@es": "Respuestas cortas: **Yes, he has.** / **No, she hasn't.**",
     "@en": "Short responses: **Yes, he has.** / **No, she hasn't.**"
    }
   ]
  },
